{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openwrt/openwrt/pulls/22397","id":3392653893,"node_id":"PR_kwDOArsuZM7KN8pF","html_url":"https://github.com/openwrt/openwrt/pull/22397","diff_url":"https://github.com/openwrt/openwrt/pull/22397.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/openwrt/openwrt/pull/22397.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openwrt/openwrt/issues/22397","commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openwrt/openwrt/pulls/22397/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openwrt/openwrt/pulls/22397/comments","review_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openwrt/openwrt/pulls/comments{/number}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openwrt/openwrt/issues/22397/comments","statuses_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openwrt/openwrt/statuses/e1fe2733a1f1b333fd25d6b0e572e0888505f9da","number":22397,"state":"open","locked":false,"title":"airoha: add support for Gemtek XR1710G","user":{"login":"hurrian","id":5042811,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUwNDI4MTE=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5042811?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/hurrian","html_url":"https://github.com/hurrian","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hurrian/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hurrian/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hurrian/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hurrian/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hurrian/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hurrian/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hurrian/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hurrian/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hurrian/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"This commit adds support for Gemtek XR1710G (Brightspeed XR1710G).\r\n\r\nSpecifications of this device are similar to the Gemtek W1700K, with some changes:\r\n- Silabs Bluetooth/Zigbee radio removed\r\n- Airoha GPS removed\r\n- MT7530 ethernet LEDs driven from switch instead of GPIO\r\n\r\nDevice specifications\r\n--------------------\r\n\r\n| | |\r\n| --- | --- |\r\n| **SoC Type** | Airoha AN7581 |\r\n| **RAM** | ESMT M16U8G16512A (2GB) |\r\n| **Flash** | Winbond 25N04KVZEIR (512MB) |\r\n| **Ethernet** | 2x gigabit via AN7581, 2x 10g via RTL8261BE |\r\n| **Wi-Fi** | MT7996 - BE19000 |\r\n| **LEDs** | 1 LED, power/status |\r\n| **Button** | Reset |\r\n| **USB ports** | None |\r\n| **Bootloader** | U-Boot 2014.04-rc1 (Mar 15 2024) AXON 1.6 |\r\n| **Fan** | 1x controlled by Nuvoton NCT7511Y |\r\n\r\nAs this device has a similar bootloader to the Gemtek W1700K, the same workarounds for BMT/BBT are needed, necessitating the U-Boot Chainloader.\r\n\r\nInstallation\r\n--------------------\r\n### 1) Connect to serial console.\r\n\r\nThere is a Torx T10 screw underneath the QR code printed onto the label. Then, pry between the gray and white\r\nplastic, starting by the ports on the back. There are clips arount the entire device.\r\n\r\nStarting closest to the screw next to the UART header:\r\n```\r\nTX - GND - VCC - N/A - RX.\r\n```\r\nThe bootloader can be interrupted by pressing any key.\r\n\r\n### 2) Configuring Vendor Bootloader and Installing U-Boot Chainloader:\r\n\r\nThe bootloader's default bootcmd will only run a signed image. However, we can still bootm our own image from flash.\r\n\r\n**NOTE:** The vendor's ethernet drivers are flaky. You may have to reboot and try the tftpboot part several times for it to work.\r\n\r\n```\r\nsetenv serverip 192.168.1.10 ; setenv ipaddr 192.168.1.1 ; tftpboot 0x89000000 openwrt-airoha-an7581-gemtek_xr1710g-ubi-chainload-uboot.itb\r\nsetenv one flash read 0x600000 0x100000 \\$loadaddr\r\nsetenv two \"; bootm\"\r\nsetenv bootcmd \"$one$two\"\r\nsaveenv\r\nflash erase 0x600000 0x100000\r\nflash write 0x600000 0x100000 0x89000000\r\nreset\r\n```\r\n\r\nThe device will now reboot into the U-Boot chainloader.\r\n\r\n### 3) Loading the UBI Installer:\r\n\r\nThe installer can be downloaded at\r\nhttps://github.com/hurrian/w1700k-ubi-installer/releases\r\n\r\n- Boot the installer via the TFTP option in the U-Boot menu. This\r\n  process is automatic, though you may be prompted to answer some\r\n  questions.\r\n- Once it is done, you may upgrade to your preferred build.\r\n- For more information: https://github.com/hurrian/w1700k-ubi-installer\r\n\r\nSigned-off-by: Kenneth Kasilag <kenneth@kasilag.me>","labels":[{"id":793819779,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWw3OTM4MTk3Nzk=","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openwrt/openwrt/labels/core%20packages","name":"core packages","description":"pull request/issue for core (in-tree) packages","color":"F5D63D","default":false},{"id":4523190557,"node_id":"LA_kwDOArsuZM8AAAABDZppHQ","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openwrt/openwrt/labels/target/airoha","name":"target/airoha","description":"pull request/issue for airoha target","color":"0043e4","default":false}],"milestone":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"created_at":"2026-03-13T01:27:59Z","updated_at":"2026-08-14T07:45:05Z","closed_at":null,"merged_at":null,"merge_commit_sha":null,"assignee":null,"assignees":[],"requested_reviewers":[],"requested_teams":[],"head":{"label":"hurrian:xr1710g","ref":"xr1710g","repo":{"id":982024727,"node_id":"R_kgDOOoiCFw","name":"openwrt-w1700k","full_name":"hurrian/openwrt-w1700k","owner":{"login":"hurrian","id":5042811,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUwNDI4MTE=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5042811?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/hurrian","html_url":"https://github.com/hurrian","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hurrian/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hurrian/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hurrian/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hurrian/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"ht